{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of","id":1199510,"title":"Time 3 Haste spell, the usefulness of","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-25T15:40:37-07:00","id":1199510,"title":"Time 3 Haste spell, the usefulness of","content":"I have a problem with the basic extra-actions-per-turn Effect that the Time sphere allows on Rank 3, namely that it seems to have no major benefit if fast-cast by a Disciple or even perhaps Adept level Mage.<br /> <br /> So, first of all, I realise that this Effect is always going to be dangerous in gameplay terms, because in a system where every character gets one action per turn under almost any circumstances, anything that will give a character more actions in a turn can potentially entirely wreck the action economy of combat. Werewolf knows this, so they gave every garou the ability to burn Rage for extra actions, but Rage is a finite and precious resource. Vampire seems to realise it to a slightly lesser extent because not everyone has Celerity and it's relatively cheap to use, but it's still limited by blood pool and the typically low blood per turn limit for most kindred. Meawhile, giving yourself an extra action per turn with Time 3 is described as coincidental(!) and doesn't necessarily cost any quintessence either so a Time Mage might theoretically give themselves two actions per turn for an entire encounter without incurring any costs if the Effect didn't have some special rules associated with it.<br /> <br /> So the rule exception applied to this Effect is that you only get one more action per turn per two successes. This means it doesn't use the Damage or Duration chart like most other spells. If it did, two successes spent on duration would be enough for a whole scene, and then an extra two turns per success spent on &quot;Damage&quot; would be... broken beyond any repair. In other words it makes sense to have that special rule in place.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately it seems to also drastically limit the usefulness of the Effect in combat unless cast by someone with Arete 6 or more. As it stands, there is no reason for a Mage of Arete 3 to ever make herself faster in combat. If she spends a point of Willpower and all three dice on that Arete roll are successes, then she would get the benefit of one extra action: the first two successes would give her one more action, making up for the one she spent casting the Effect, and the other two would give her a bonus action. She would not be allowed to use either of those actions to create another Effect, however. Three successes or less on that roll will just replace the action she spent casting the Effect, and that's pointless. This leaves the only real utility of the Effect as a way to &quot;give&quot; your action to someone else, eg. if another group member has a higher damage output than you, haste them so they can attack twice at the cost of you spending your action to do that.<br /> <br /> Now... on Time 4 you get to hang your Effects, meaning you could haste yourself as a ritual and hang it for when the shit hits the fan. Similarly, you could make a haste Charm with Prime 2 so you can accumulate a bunch of successes in the crafting and activate it easily later, for example giving yourself an extra action per turn for three turns in a row upon activation. But doesn't it seem kind of odd that the benefit of hasting yourself in a fight is basically null? It's a rank 3 Effect after all, other spheres give you some pretty crazy abilities on that level.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to hear what you guys think, how you or your players have been using it, and if you even agree with how I interpret the rules - or even whether you agree with the rules themselves.<br /> <br /> I'd also be interested to hear how you deal with speeding up or slowing down people or objects outside of combat: do you use the Damage/Duration chart for that? If a Time Mage wants to speed up his car on the way to taking his bleeding friend to the hospital, do you ask for two successes to be spent on Duration and then double the speed of the car for each further success spent on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:19:06-07:00","id":1199524,"title":"","content":"Just make it vulgar and worry less. If you\u2019re going to make changes, that would be the obvious one to make.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I\u2019m surprised to hear it wasn\u2019t vulgar. I\u2019d always assumed that for this effect to be coincidental, it would have to speed you up quite marginally, not enough to give you an extra turn, but perhaps enough to lower the difficulty for things like attacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 03-25-2018, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T17:02:48-07:00","id":1199539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199524#post1199524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make it vulgar and worry less. If you\u2019re going to make changes, that would be the obvious one to make.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I\u2019m surprised to hear it wasn\u2019t vulgar. I\u2019d always assumed that for this effect to be coincidental, it would have to speed you up quite marginally, not enough to give you an extra turn, but perhaps enough to lower the difficulty for things like attacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people are just that fast. Look at an experienced martial artist or athlete, and you can see them doing multiple &quot;actions&quot; per &quot;turn&quot;. Turns in WoD take roughly 3 seconds. In reality, three seconds is a long time in the thick of combat. This is why in the game, when splitting dice pools, a skilled combatant (with lots of Attribute and Ability dots) can still be fairly effective taking an extra action, even two.<br /> <br /> So if a mage uses Time 3 to give them a couple extra actions, it's entirely reasonable for it to be coincidental. The Coincidental/Vulgar idea is tied to what seems plausible, not to what would make for the most balanced gameplay.<br /> <br /> Then again, &quot;Balance&quot; is overrated. Especially with WoD combat at base being as deadly as it is, even before supernatural powers are brought into the picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T00:18:46-07:00","id":1199615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199539#post1199539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people are just that fast. Look at an experienced martial artist or athlete, and you can see them doing multiple &quot;actions&quot; per &quot;turn&quot;. Turns in WoD take roughly 3 seconds. In reality, three seconds is a long time in the thick of combat. This is why in the game, when splitting dice pools, a skilled combatant (with lots of Attribute and Ability dots) can still be fairly effective taking an extra action, even two.<br /> <br /> So if a mage uses Time 3 to give them a couple extra actions, it's entirely reasonable for it to be coincidental. The Coincidental/Vulgar idea is tied to what seems plausible, not to what would make for the most balanced gameplay.<br /> <br /> Then again, &quot;Balance&quot; is overrated. Especially with WoD combat at base being as deadly as it is, even before supernatural powers are brought into the picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can take multiple actions in a turn. It just makes the difficulty shoot right up.<br /> <br /> The vulgar part is where you look to be moving at fast forward speeds.<br /> I.e. taking multiple actions without the penalty it usually affords.<br /> <br /> Some people may be just that fast, but not so fast that they look like a sped up video. If you watc a YouTube video at 2x speed, you\u2019ll see just how unnatural the movement is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T01:26:19-07:00","id":1199631,"title":"","content":"I would say that one extra action could be coincidental. Anything above that would incur paradox. Also, you could limit it to only allowing up to Wits or Dex actions per turn. Anything above that would not be possible as the characters brain or body would not be able to cope with such changes to the normal timeflow. This has been (or still is, can't remember) a rule for Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Ofc this could be countered by adding Life or Mind to the Time 3 spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T01:32:04-07:00","id":1199634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199524#post1199524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make it vulgar and worry less. If you\u2019re going to make changes, that would be the obvious one to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how that's supposed to solve anything :P<br /> <br /> My problem is that under the current rules, the Effect is largely useless in combat until you can cast it with a really high Arete. Making it vulgar will only make it even more useless still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T04:11:39-07:00","id":1199651,"title":"","content":"Okay so here's the actual text from the book, I just re-read it to make sure I remembered it correctly, and now that I see it again, I'm not sure I interpreted it correctly the first time around:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> every two successes allow the character to take one additional action that does not involve casting magick (only one Arete roll may be made per turn); or else slow another character, object, or even herself down by one increment per success. (Four successes, for example, would slow a person down to a quarter of his normal speed.) </div> </div> </div>I read this in the way that you get one extra action per two successes, so if you wanted an extra action this turn and an extra action next turn, you'd need four successes. But that's not really stated, so I think that interpretation just happened in my brain because the alternative seemed too powerful to imagine. So it's quite possible that they actually mean for the normal duration of the spell. Meaning four successes would give you an extra action per turn for the entire rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> In that case, the spell definitely has utility, in fact it just may have <i>too much</i> utility. Making it vulgar would help a little, but not enough to make it not by far the best option to use this spell for every fight. Then again, rolling four successes during combat is hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T04:23:39-07:00","id":1199652,"title":"","content":"I'd just make it vulgar.<br /> Let time do it coincidentally with a different effect that cancels flurry penalties / adds dice to flurried pools up to their original pool limit. Bam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umsakis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199651#post1199651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read this in the way that you get one extra action per two successes, so if you wanted an extra action this turn and an extra action next turn, you'd need four successes. But that's not really stated, so I think that interpretation just happened in my brain because the alternative seemed too powerful to imagine. So it's quite possible that they actually mean for the normal duration of the spell. Meaning four successes would give you an extra action per turn for the entire rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> In that case, the spell definitely has utility, in fact it just may have <i>too much</i> utility. Making it vulgar would help a little, but not enough to make it not by far the best option to use this spell for every fight. Then again, rolling four successes during combat is hard.</div> </div> </div> </div> I let the effect apply itself every round for the duration. It's powerful, but it doesn't break the game any more than the other action multipliers. If one is allowed, no reason not to allow the other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 03-26-2018, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T04:35:31-07:00","id":1199655,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say it lasts per scene, and allow extra successes to make it last for extra scenes rather than for a day or for 6 months.<br /> <br /> With the caveat that every extra scenes adds to the paradox incurred citing that time magic is intrinsically paradox heavy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:20:16-07:00","id":1199662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199631#post1199631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you could limit it to only allowing up to Wits or Dex actions per turn. Anything above that would not be possible as the characters brain or body would not be able to cope with such changes to the normal timeflow. This has been (or still is, can't remember) a rule for Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Ofc this could be countered by adding Life or Mind to the Time 3 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and I don't think it really applies, as essentially everything around you slows down to your perceptions - you move at normal speed, so there technically is no overloading of the senses.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd go with the suggestion of making anything past 1 extra action vulgar. Somebody pulling of damn good stuff with two actions a round? Excusable. But becomign a blur of 2-3 actions nonstop? Suspiccccioussss...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:22:43-07:00","id":1199664,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot guys, I'll try playing with it that way and seeing how it works out. Considering Mages aren't typically the biggest badasses at mundane combat (I have no Akashayana in my group) and you can still only create 1 Effect per turn no matter how fast you're going, I guess it may be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:33:44-07:00","id":1199669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umsakis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199664#post1199664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot guys, I'll try playing with it that way and seeing how it works out. Considering Mages aren't typically the biggest badasses at mundane combat (I have no Akashayana in my group) and you can still only create 1 Effect per turn no matter how fast you're going, I guess it may be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the primary reason it doesn't break the game any harder than the others do. Realistically a chargen mage is wasting his time improvising that, and is at high risk of botching if he prepares it beforehand for prolonged use (plus the persistent paradox and later pattern bleeding).<br /> <br /> A mage that went through a couple quests and carries his weight as a veteran runs much lower risk, but still won't usually have a scene long buff for more than a couple actions. At this point creatures making him work for his money will pull off the same on top of anything else they might do.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Time combatant is usually better off with other alternatives if one wants to use such effects liberally, such as slowing down the opponent or circumventing problems like &quot;numerical disadvantage&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:50:25-07:00","id":1199675,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a simple double-action buff wouldn't at the very least eliminate the fast-casting penalty though. Since your spell difficulty is reduced by 1 per extra turn you spend on it, seems like if you have two actions per turn and spend both of them on the spell, you'd get rid of that penalty. That's not a game-breaking advantage by any means, but it'd certainly be a nice little bonus. Alternatively it lets the Mage defend against enemy physical attacks and cast spells at the same time, with no split dice pool (and splitting your dice pool for magick is incredibly punishing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T08:53:55-07:00","id":1199725,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d argue not. Even though you feel like you\u2019re acting at normal speed, everything else around is slower, so the casting would also be slower.<br /> <br /> If you were tapping out an effect on a computer, you\u2019d still have to wait for the computer to register your input and execute it. You\u2019d still have to wait for the music you play to affect your target, the angels to hear your request and respond, or the crystals in your energy gun to warm up and build up the charge.<br /> <br /> It would still require fast casting in order to enact your will quickly above the time delay that similarly limits you to one effect per turn.<br /> <br /> Also, the fewer bits and pieces that need to be altered for standard rotes, the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:01:24-07:00","id":1199747,"title":"","content":"Well, computers are so fast, somebody typing at even four times the speed wouldn't even matter to it.<br /> <br /> But, yes, Time 3 would still not be able to negate fast-casting penalties, since the books point out that the 'flow' of Magick, it's rate, is constant. it cannot be accelerated or slowed down with Time Magick - you spending two Time 3 turns on casting still would result in you trying to cast Magick in but a few seconds. Same reason why, even with 8 free actions, you can only cast Magick once in a whole combat turn (ignoring, as usual, additional sources of casts, like wonders).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-26-2018, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:24:31-07:00","id":1199752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199747#post1199747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(ignoring, as usual, additional sources of casts, like wonders).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, only wonders with their own arete could be invoked in this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:15:16-07:00","id":1199768,"title":"","content":"Yup, hence sources. Any source of Arete can only cast once per normal amount of time, no matter how fast that source can act.<br /> <br /> ...I now actually wonder what happens to an Arete-holding Wonder if the Mage who made it dies. In theory, the magick of the wonder works through the creator's avatar...the avatar remains after death and inhabits a new sleeper (or potential mage).<br /> I wonder if that person would be drawn to the wonder made by their predecessor. Worth noting down for a potential plot!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T13:41:05-07:00","id":1199821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199655#post1199655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say it lasts per scene, and allow extra successes to make it last for extra scenes rather than for a day or for 6 months.<br /> <br /> With the caveat that every extra scenes adds to the paradox incurred citing that time magic is intrinsically paradox heavy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is it written that Time Magick has a tendency to result in additional Paradox for the casting Mage(s) , in comparison to other kinds of Magick ? Could you give more than one source for this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-26-2018, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T13:45:11-07:00","id":1199823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199821#post1199821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is it written that Time Magick has a tendency to result in additional Paradox for the casting Mage(s) , in comparison to other kinds of Magick ? Could you give more than one source for this ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reversing time for instance gives you two points per turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T04:10:15-07:00","id":1199979,"title":"","content":"How confident are we that the fast-casting penalty in combat comes from some kind of universal flow speed of magick? It's my distinct impression that it's just meant to represent the difficulty of having to use your instruments to do complicated things while somebody is trying to murder you. The rule that Effects that use a weapon for a focus are not subject to a fast-casting penalty would seem to support this. In which case, speeding yourself up and then using the extra time to take more care in the use of your instruments would make sense as well, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T07:57:38-07:00","id":1200035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Umsakis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199979#post1199979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule that Effects that use a weapon for a focus are not subject to a fast-casting penalty would seem to support this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a good point, all said.<br /> Of course another balancing factor would be the fact, that if you use Time 3 to spend more time on pulling off an effect, everybody else acts before you do, so unless you pull off a lot of extra turns (and thus go vulgar with Time), you need to be in a very defensive position in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:18:47-07:00","id":1200148,"title":"","content":"As always, a mage\u2019s chance in battle is wholly dependant on preparation time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T01:37:48-07:00","id":1200373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1200035#post1200035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course another balancing factor would be the fact, that if you use Time 3 to spend more time on pulling off an effect, everybody else acts before you do, so unless you pull off a lot of extra turns (and thus go vulgar with Time), you need to be in a very defensive position in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true. Might not be too OP then. I'll try it out in practice and see how it goes.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for all your input, both of you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23636-umsakis","name":"Umsakis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:28:07-07:00","id":1200815,"title":"","content":"My mage currently uses time 3 haste by doing a short rite ( 5 minutes cast time with cap of 5 successes ) to get 2 extra actions per round for the scene before going into combat. That combined with a greatsword thats a 5 dot wonder makes them about as nasty as a frenzied brujah in a straight up fight. If you have arete 4 you could cast the effect and pull it forward till you get the full 4 successes and then simply concentrate on keeping the effect going untill you no longer need it, which means you can get the 2 extra action without dedicating to duration as long as you keep concentration. Concentrating on effects to keep them going is talked about on page 528 under &quot;How Many Effects Can I Use At Once?&quot;. For a non-physical mage, the extra time actions can be used for other things, like dodge actions or whatever else you might be doing in or out of combat ( My same mage uses this to create artwork twice as fast ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23906-alzuule","name":"Alzuule","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:07:26-07:00","id":1201374,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't <i>Time 3 - haste</i> (faster actions) and <i>Time 3 - extra actions </i>be separate Effects ? I think that they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T17:41:59-07:00","id":1201484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1201374#post1201374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't <i>Time 3 - haste</i> (faster actions) and <i>Time 3 - extra actions </i>be separate Effects ? I think that they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div> How exactly do you distinguish between the two?<br /> <br /> If you're doing things faster, it would take fewer turns to get done.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T09:23:07-07:00","id":1202240,"title":"","content":"Well, the first question is how is it any more imbalanced than being able to reduce difficulties via Time (or, really, any applicable sphere) level 1 and splitting dice pool three ways from Sunday? Do it as an extended Effect, and you can buffer the lost potential successes per-roll (to translate to overage, or maximize defensive successes) via fast casts on a per-turn basis.<br /> <br /> The last Akashic I played, had a Perception + Do dice pool of ten. She had Legendary Attribute (Perception), I'd use a Mind rote to buff it to six, and swap Perception for Dexterity on relevant rolls. Her &quot;legendary attribute ability&quot; was a stripped-down version of Auspex 1 danger sense, so I'd reliably have a round or two before combat started to buff. <i>Then</i>, I'd use the aforementioned Time Effect, allowing me to take five actions per round, all at difficulty 3. Completely coincidentally. Her attack and defense dice pools left much to be desired, sure, but she also had Forces to buff raw damage/soak values as needed.<br /> <br /> Considering what else is possible in the context of MtAs, the notion of extra actions via Time 3 -- and the impracticality of doing it on the fly -- is pretty quaint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 04-02-2018, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:53:12-07:00","id":1204492,"title":"","content":"Time has always felt like the least relevant Sphere to me. Time travel is just not a practical use of effort and is bad for your health. Multiple actions seem like more effort than they are worth. &quot;Hanging&quot; magick until certain conditions are met is very nice, and extending effects for a long time is cool, but is it worth all the EXP? And Time 2 would be the best investigative power ever if the books didn't tell STs to go &quot;um no&quot; whenever they don't feel like Time 2 telling you what it should in terms of looking back in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T04:15:35-07:00","id":1204498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1204492#post1204492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time has always felt like the least relevant Sphere to me. Time travel is just not a practical use of effort and is bad for your health. Multiple actions seem like more effort than they are worth. &quot;Hanging&quot; magick until certain conditions are met is very nice, and extending effects for a long time is cool, but is it worth all the EXP? And Time 2 would be the best investigative power ever if the books didn't tell STs to go &quot;um no&quot; whenever they don't feel like Time 2 telling you what it should in terms of looking back in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Time 4 stopping capability is extremely useful, especially considering that such Effects can be used Coincidentally in many situations. Sometimes machines don't work and cease to function. A lock might get stuck - or a key which is linked with many other keys gets stuck in a lock. Many items and situations with hidden or unseen parts and circumstances involved can be stopped with Time 4 Coincidentally. The Vulgar Time 4 stopping capability seems very powerful and very useful to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-08-2018, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T04:35:04-07:00","id":1204503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1204498#post1204498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Time 4 stopping capability is extremely useful, especially considering that such Effects can be used Coincidentally in many situations. Sometimes machines don't work and cease to function. A lock might get stuck - or a key which is linked with many other keys gets stuck in a lock. Many items and situations with hidden or unseen parts and circumstances involved can be stopped with Time 4 Coincidentally. The Vulgar Time 4 stopping capability seems very powerful and very useful to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh certainly, but the Spheres are so wide that a few impressive and great abilities are going to get drowned out. Stopping time is cool, freezing objects in time is great, but at Spirit 4 you're sailing the great unknown in the Umbra, and at Matter 4 you are generating feather-light armour with amazing soak, and at Mind 4 the emotions and beliefs of most people can be shaped and redirected. And Forces 4 pushes you into &quot;directing a forest fire&quot; levels of awesome, while Prime is an incredible toolkit at all levels and Life has you pushing your body to impossible feats.<br /> <br /> So it's not that Time is BAD. Time is awesome. But it's competing with some really really incredible Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-08-2018, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:01:24-07:00","id":1204507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1199768#post1199768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, hence sources. Any source of Arete can only cast once per normal amount of time, no matter how fast that source can act.<br /> <br /> ...I now actually wonder what happens to an Arete-holding Wonder if the Mage who made it dies. In theory, the magick of the wonder works through the creator's avatar...the avatar remains after death and inhabits a new sleeper (or potential mage).<br /> I wonder if that person would be drawn to the wonder made by their predecessor. Worth noting down for a potential plot!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's such a great idea! This Mage PC is a newbie, much weaker than the other PCs (only a few dots of Spheres), but has Avatar 5 and their Arete is going up fast. The Mage who used to have their Avatar was a friend of all of the PCs, and was a de facto leader, respected, powerful, missed. And all of their Wonders are still lying around, waiting to be found!<br /> <br /> And of course you can make it quite dark. Finding a Wonder with your own Resonance which is for doing something pretty horrible, discovering your own Avatar has a dark past...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:22:08-07:00","id":1204510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1204503#post1204503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh certainly, but the Spheres are so wide that a few impressive and great abilities are going to get drowned out. Stopping time is cool, freezing objects in time is great, but at Spirit 4 you're sailing the great unknown in the Umbra, and at Matter 4 you are generating feather-light armour with amazing soak, and at Mind 4 the emotions and beliefs of most people can be shaped and redirected. And Forces 4 pushes you into &quot;directing a forest fire&quot; levels of awesome, while Prime is an incredible toolkit at all levels and Life has you pushing your body to impossible feats.<br /> <br /> So it's not that Time is BAD. Time is awesome. But it's competing with some really really incredible Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>It all depends on the ST.<br /> <br /> Prime, for example, is terrible if the ST isn't willing to put a bunch of quintessence in their game like Nodes or Tass. Similarly for Spirit, if the ST isn't all that familiar on WoD spirits, or even spirit lore itself, this sphere can be a huge drag to use, and forget about gallivanting off into the umbra if your ST isn't equipped to deal with that.<br /> <br /> If any of my players chose the Time sphere, then just like is someone chose Spirit or Prime, I would be adding a whole host of content in there for them. I'd introduce the world of Time mages, mages that sit outside the boundries of time and manipulate things completely unseen and only even detectable by Time 1. I'd have creatures living in the corners between time, such as the hounds of tindaols or other such bizarre beings. I'd introduce ripples in the time stream, fluctuations where areas are slightly out of sync with the &quot;natural flow&quot;, areas around nodes or even strange locations where time just halts for a brief second. These are areas where the arrow of time is curved, where the river of time forms eddies, or where the cracks in time form, depending on your mage's paradigm regarding how time works.<br /> Again, only detectable via Time 1. Time 2 might allow one to look upon these phenomena and investigate what they are, perhaps they are future or past echos, points of repetition which are doomed for repeat, or even an act of Time 4 magic down centuries past just waiting to go off when the right conditions align.<br /> <br /> And don't let me hear anyone dissing Time 2. It is by far the single most broken rank 2 sphere rank in the game. I abused the hell out of it when I was playing a time mage, it allowed me to know exactly what had happened in every mystery setting we had encountered, see what could possibly happen if we chose various paths (avoiding stupid decisions), follow people long after the trail had gone cold, learn if someone was still in the place we saw them enter, and even discover the possible answers of centuries old questions.<br /> <br /> My ST really should not have given me this much power. They ended up dreading every time I started rolling for it as it would, as they put it, ruin all the suspense that they were trying to build up. I just knew everything so there were no real surprises and we were almost always prepared for everything. But then, their mistakes will help me balance this thing if it ever comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T05:48:59-07:00","id":1204513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1204510#post1204510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It all depends on the ST.<br /> <br /> Prime, for example, is terrible if the ST isn't willing to put a bunch of quintessence in their game like Nodes or Tass. Similarly for Spirit, if the ST isn't all that familiar on WoD spirits, or even spirit lore itself, this sphere can be a huge drag to use, and forget about gallivanting off into the umbra if your ST isn't equipped to deal with that.<br /> <br /> If any of my players chose the Time sphere, then just like is someone chose Spirit or Prime, I would be adding a whole host of content in there for them. I'd introduce the world of Time mages, mages that sit outside the boundries of time and manipulate things completely unseen and only even detectable by Time 1. I'd have creatures living in the corners between time, such as the hounds of tindaols or other such bizarre beings. I'd introduce ripples in the time stream, fluctuations where areas are slightly out of sync with the &quot;natural flow&quot;, areas around nodes or even strange locations where time just halts for a brief second. These are areas where the arrow of time is curved, where the river of time forms eddies, or where the cracks in time form, depending on your mage's paradigm regarding how time works.<br /> Again, only detectable via Time 1. Time 2 might allow one to look upon these phenomena and investigate what they are, perhaps they are future or past echos, points of repetition which are doomed for repeat, or even an act of Time 4 magic down centuries past just waiting to go off when the right conditions align.<br /> <br /> And don't let me hear anyone dissing Time 2. It is by far the single most broken rank 2 sphere rank in the game. I abused the hell out of it when I was playing a time mage, it allowed me to know exactly what had happened in every mystery setting we had encountered, see what could possibly happen if we chose various paths (avoiding stupid decisions), follow people long after the trail had gone cold, learn if someone was still in the place we saw them enter, and even discover the possible answers of centuries old questions.<br /> <br /> My ST really should not have given me this much power. They ended up dreading every time I started rolling for it as it would, as they put it, ruin all the suspense that they were trying to build up. I just knew everything so there were no real surprises and we were almost always prepared for everything. But then, their mistakes will help me balance this thing if it ever comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I suppose the issue is that many Paradigms accept Ghosts and Demons etc. but many Paradigms struggle with &quot;weird time&quot;. Virtual adepts, for example, stick with Time 2 and predictions and looking at the past, modeling events, rather than weird blips in the flow of time for example. The Technocracy considers most vulgar applications of Time to be a kind of reality deviance, and that makes Time a dangerous and antisocial tool in a Technocracy game. And a background in Wraith or Vampire or Demon or Werewolf will leave an ST competent in terms of dealing with Spirits, but nothing will prepare you for weird time oddities in Mage terms IMO.<br /> <br /> As for sources of Quintessence, reading M20 there are so many sources that I don't think you need Nodes at all. All living creatures, every Business (with Primal Utility), every supernatural being, every Spirit, even the universe itself with higher levels of Prime (though that may be vulgar) is a good source of Quintessence if you work at it.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, Time 2 can be extremely powerful, if the ST is playing it that way. But M20 makes it crystal clear that Time 2 should be vague and filled with hints, and should not give much clarity. It warns that Time 2 can be a &quot;plot breaker&quot; and says that you should be careful with the information you give out. And honestly, that's probably a good idea if there's meant to be some mystery or complex problem solving.<br /> <br /> I think that problems with Time, Mages who exist outside of Time, anomalies with Time... you're right. A lot of it comes down to a specific ST. But Stepping Sideways is always useful (unless there's an AVATAR STORM that is inconsiderately blocking your path...), even if an ST really knows very little about the Umbra. If nothing else, it's a &quot;I want to leave&quot; power which gets you out of tight spots. Time at 3+ feels like a situational counter and a powerful plot solver. Spirit at 3+ is a situational counter and powerful plot solver, and it's also just useful in normal ways. And the same is true of Prime, naturally. It's useful when you need to completely drain and then close a Node which is bursting with toxic Quintessence after being corrupted by some Nephandi or Black Spiral Dancers, and it's also useful when you just need to get some Quintessence out of a retainer or enchant an object from your Avatar's guaranteed Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T07:08:29-07:00","id":1204536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1204513#post1204513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I suppose the issue is that many Paradigms accept Ghosts and Demons etc. but many Paradigms struggle with &quot;weird time&quot;. Virtual adepts, for example, stick with Time 2 and predictions and looking at the past, modeling events, rather than weird blips in the flow of time for example. The Technocracy considers most vulgar applications of Time to be a kind of reality deviance, and that makes Time a dangerous and antisocial tool in a Technocracy game. And a background in Wraith or Vampire or Demon or Werewolf will leave an ST competent in terms of dealing with Spirits, but nothing will prepare you for weird time oddities in Mage terms IMO.<br /> <br /> As for sources of Quintessence, reading M20 there are so many sources that I don't think you need Nodes at all. All living creatures, every Business (with Primal Utility), every supernatural being, every Spirit, even the universe itself with higher levels of Prime (though that may be vulgar) is a good source of Quintessence if you work at it.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, Time 2 can be extremely powerful, if the ST is playing it that way. But M20 makes it crystal clear that Time 2 should be vague and filled with hints, and should not give much clarity. It warns that Time 2 can be a &quot;plot breaker&quot; and says that you should be careful with the information you give out. And honestly, that's probably a good idea if there's meant to be some mystery or complex problem solving.<br /> <br /> I think that problems with Time, Mages who exist outside of Time, anomalies with Time... you're right. A lot of it comes down to a specific ST. But Stepping Sideways is always useful (unless there's an AVATAR STORM that is inconsiderately blocking your path...), even if an ST really knows very little about the Umbra. If nothing else, it's a &quot;I want to leave&quot; power which gets you out of tight spots. Time at 3+ feels like a situational counter and a powerful plot solver. Spirit at 3+ is a situational counter and powerful plot solver, and it's also just useful in normal ways. And the same is true of Prime, naturally. It's useful when you need to completely drain and then close a Node which is bursting with toxic Quintessence after being corrupted by some Nephandi or Black Spiral Dancers, and it's also useful when you just need to get some Quintessence out of a retainer or enchant an object from your Avatar's guaranteed Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're still relying on your ST to have sufficient knowledge in how resonance, how it affects nodes, how it affects mages, the magic that is works with, how it interacts with the avatar.... You're also relying on your ST to remember every little detail in that massive tome of a book which, realistically, may not happen in the heat of a game.<br /> <br /> Regarding spirit, it's not just that you need familiarity with the background of Wraith or Werewolf to let the spirit sphere work, you need familiarity with ALL of those books, otherwise the ST will have to tell the player &quot;no&quot; at key points. I'm going to go into the valley of the dead, and then to the afterworlds of the high umbra before jumping off of Jupiter's Moons into a portal that leads to the Digital Web... What? No!? Why? What kind of Mage game is this?!<br /> <br /> Or even, &quot;I want to play a Euthanatos who often visits the Dark Umbra and has a regular contact within a Stygian governed citadel... What do you mean you never read Wraith?&quot;<br /> <br /> Even the concept of Videre makes the act of stepping sideways somewhat of a confusion if your ST isn't fully aware of it. The spirit world is vast and confounding, and not even the information provided by M20 is barely enough to allow someone the information required to get to grips with it all. And unless you're willing to railroad the entire thing, you have to be prepared for the player to try and get to specific bits of it.<br /> <br /> On top of that, there's the way that magic works in the different realms of the spirit world, how paradox functions, which spheres work differently and how, which paradigms are considered coincidental and which are not, whether certain places are even possible for certain mages to access... And the best part is the information isn't even in one specific book, but scattered across at least 5 different books, all of which are necessary to at least review if you want a comprehensive understanding of the way the spirit world functions.<br /> <br /> Either that or you ST has to make it all up, which is absolutely fine, but then why not make stuff up for the other spheres as well?<br /> <br /> Regarding the Time sphere. I really don't think the technocracy is as &quot;against&quot; time as you're making them out to be. The Void Engineers have a specific group of chrononauts which take regular voyages through time, and Time magic is often used by both Iteration X and N.W.O for various reasons such as performance upgrades, time tables and schedules, Conditional operations, and fixing errors. Extrapolating outwards, I bet you anything there is a group of N.W.O agents who specialise in men in black style time fixes, ensuring that knowledge of time travel and such never reaches the public outside of their control. Such departments in the year 2550 may even use a large number of Time related gadgets to prevent the world from falling away from the &quot;alpha&quot; time line. However, they must be very very discreet on how they do this in order to remain completely undiscovered.<br /> <br /> As for Time 3, it isn't just a &quot;gain extra turns&quot; or &quot;Undo mistakes&quot; kind of power. You can also speed and slow down objects and areas. You can slow down you opponent to a crawl, you can make a car speed up without affecting the physics of it, you can slow down the death of someone while you get them out of harms way, slow down a crumbling wall or the water falling from it, slow down bullets making it possible to doge, speed up your sword thrusts making it harder to parry.<br /> With other spheres you could slow down light around your opponents face making it hard to see what's going on, reverse the breaking of your bones, reverse someone's mind to before they were in a coma, slow down someone's thoughts so they are unable to react in time, speed up the rate of quintessence flow, slow down the decay of a collapsing building.<br /> <br /> Like any sphere, it requires imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:07:58-07:00","id":1204575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1199510-time-3-haste-spell-the-usefulness-of?p=1204536#post1204536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're still relying on your ST to have sufficient knowledge in how resonance, how it affects nodes, how it affects mages, the magic that is works with, how it interacts with the avatar.... You're also relying on your ST to remember every little detail in that massive tome of a book which, realistically, may not happen in the heat of a game.<br /> <br /> Regarding spirit, it's not just that you need familiarity with the background of Wraith or Werewolf to let the spirit sphere work, you need familiarity with ALL of those books, otherwise the ST will have to tell the player &quot;no&quot; at key points. I'm going to go into the valley of the dead, and then to the afterworlds of the high umbra before jumping off of Jupiter's Moons into a portal that leads to the Digital Web... What? No!? Why? What kind of Mage game is this?!<br /> <br /> Or even, &quot;I want to play a Euthanatos who often visits the Dark Umbra and has a regular contact within a Stygian governed citadel... What do you mean you never read Wraith?&quot;<br /> <br /> Even the concept of Videre makes the act of stepping sideways somewhat of a confusion if your ST isn't fully aware of it. The spirit world is vast and confounding, and not even the information provided by M20 is barely enough to allow someone the information required to get to grips with it all. And unless you're willing to railroad the entire thing, you have to be prepared for the player to try and get to specific bits of it.<br /> <br /> On top of that, there's the way that magic works in the different realms of the spirit world, how paradox functions, which spheres work differently and how, which paradigms are considered coincidental and which are not, whether certain places are even possible for certain mages to access... And the best part is the information isn't even in one specific book, but scattered across at least 5 different books, all of which are necessary to at least review if you want a comprehensive understanding of the way the spirit world functions.<br /> <br /> Either that or you ST has to make it all up, which is absolutely fine, but then why not make stuff up for the other spheres as well?<br /> <br /> Regarding the Time sphere. I really don't think the technocracy is as &quot;against&quot; time as you're making them out to be. The Void Engineers have a specific group of chrononauts which take regular voyages through time, and Time magic is often used by both Iteration X and N.W.O for various reasons such as performance upgrades, time tables and schedules, Conditional operations, and fixing errors. Extrapolating outwards, I bet you anything there is a group of N.W.O agents who specialise in men in black style time fixes, ensuring that knowledge of time travel and such never reaches the public outside of their control. Such departments in the year 2550 may even use a large number of Time related gadgets to prevent the world from falling away from the &quot;alpha&quot; time line. However, they must be very very discreet on how they do this in order to remain completely undiscovered.<br /> <br /> As for Time 3, it isn't just a &quot;gain extra turns&quot; or &quot;Undo mistakes&quot; kind of power. You can also speed and slow down objects and areas. You can slow down you opponent to a crawl, you can make a car speed up without affecting the physics of it, you can slow down the death of someone while you get them out of harms way, slow down a crumbling wall or the water falling from it, slow down bullets making it possible to doge, speed up your sword thrusts making it harder to parry.<br /> With other spheres you could slow down light around your opponents face making it hard to see what's going on, reverse the breaking of your bones, reverse someone's mind to before they were in a coma, slow down someone's thoughts so they are unable to react in time, speed up the rate of quintessence flow, slow down the decay of a collapsing building.<br /> <br /> Like any sphere, it requires imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>- A lot of the complex and esoteric applications of Prime ask a lot of the ST, yes. However the simple applications are manifold and incredibly useful. I'm arguing that in terms of Spirit, Prime and Time, the former two have a greater variety of simple applications which are more useful on average.<br /> <br /> - Yes, the Spirit world is really complicated and the ST needs to know a lot to truly give the &quot;WoD Umbra Experience&quot;. However stuff like exorcism, stepping sideways, fighting spirits, draining Quintessence from spirits with Prime/Spirit, talking with ghosts... it doesn't ask that much, and even THAT on its own is incredibly useful. So even a novice Mage ST will give you a lot of useful stuff with Spirit.<br /> <br /> - My main point was that some paradigms really struggle with the more esoteric applications of Time, because of Vulgarity. I'm sure there are VAs who &quot;hack time&quot;, generating buggy parts of reality with temporal anomalies (feels a bit Technephandi), and of course the Void Engineers like a bit of Time with their Dimensional Science and their Correspondence. However the best applications of Time will always be incredibly Vulgar, and a tad antisocial. Terrible things happen to wizards who mess with time Harry.<br /> <br /> - I've never actually STed Mage outside of some brief text stuff, so I can't say this with authority, but most of these feel Vulgar, and also sound like they could be achieved Coincidentally with other Spheres, saving EXP and avoiding Paradox. If someone slips into &quot;bullet time&quot; while everyone else is moving normally, or looks like they're running through treacle, that's really Vulgar in all Reality Zones honestly. Even in the most mystical magical parts of the world where people believe in spirits and magic, someone who looks like they're sprinting moving at a slow pace is not Coincidental. A Forces/Matter effect where your incredibly suped up car suddenly blasts out Nitrous and flies down the street? Coincidental. An ordinary looking car moving at 160 when it logically shouldn't get past 80? Could be Vulgar. If you're using Time to slow down a Sleeper's death, then that's going to be Vulgar, as they perceive the rest of the universe speeding up. Unless they're really far gone, in which case they might interpret it as blood loss or brain damage. Slowing down bullets, matrix style? Vulgar. Dodging those bullets &quot;entirely by chance&quot;, or your thick leather jacket stopping the bullets from properly harming you, should usually be coincidental. You get the idea.<br /> <br /> Tl;dr Time is situationally a powerful plot device (dealing with other Mages who are creating Plot using Time), and has a few powerful effects which are worthwhile (extra actions for example), and a bunch of potent effects which are highly Vulgar (slowing others down to a halt), and a few really tempting and awesome effects which are so Vulgar and difficult they're almost invariably pointless (time travel, rewinding time unless it's life or death).<br /> <br /> When compared to a Sphere like Mind, which is a situationally powerful plot device (needing it to unwind the Pattern of a &quot;memory worm&quot; which eats people's pasts) AND has many great coincidental applications (small illusions, reading surface thoughts, projecting simple ideas, processing huge amounts of data, boosting your Mental attributes), AND has a few potent and Vulgar uses (making a sleeper your thrall, reading deep into a person's mind, generating powerful AI), I don't really think there's much competition.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say that I hate Time, I just feel like it's the least powerful or useful out of 9 sets of really impressive powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-08-2018, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:42:31-07:00","id":1204619,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> <br /> <br /> First thing to point out is that coincidental magic is all about circumstance. What was coincidental in one situation will be very vulgar in another. A car moving at 160, totally could happen, coincidental. But in the presence of a mottorhead sleeper, and it's their car you're time speeding. Vulgar with a witness. Slowing down a sleeper's death? Should be fine, they don't know what's going on, perhaps when you're close to death this is just how it feels to be leaving your body behind. &quot;I felt like time just.... flew passed me... but at the same time... everything was very still....&quot; Done on the operating table though, while doctors are watching... that could be suspicious.<br /> <br /> Again, it's all about imagination and ingenuity.<br /> <br /> The problem with Mind is that it is very difficult to do anything big with Mind until the higher levels. Mind 1 and 2 are almost entierly sensory, while only at Mind 3 do you get to flex your command muscles. Your memory worm technique would be a Mind 4 rote on its own, but arguably you could also have a &quot;brain freeze&quot; effect with Time 3 and Mind 1. (your ST may vary. That's what I'd allow at least). There's also the extra caveat that Mind magic can be Willpowered away fairly easily at low levels. You either need to make a very big effect, or be a very powerful mage in order to disregard the target's willpower entirely.<br /> <br /> Also, coincidental does not necessarily mean more useful. In fact I've seen my players get into a hell of a lot of trouble because they tried a whole bunch of things in an attempt to be coincidental, when one good vulgar effect would have solved a lot of problems.<br /> <br /> I agree that Time magic tends to be more paradox inviting than the other spheres. Every single sphere has some quirk to it. Prime needs quintessence to power many of its effects, Spirit deals with the gauntlet, Matter has more permanence than the other spheres, Forces is really painful and volatile, Mind is more coincidental than other spheres but has less permanence, Life can result in pattern bleed, Corr. magic augments your range, but makes it easier to trace you back. Entropy becomes less likely to work the more you use it, and Time is a paradox magnet.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}